---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="Privacy policy for geographyofcrime.com.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap stack prose">
      <p class="label">Privacy · Last updated October 2026</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">This site collects as little as possible.</p>

      <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No cookies, no advertising, and no tracking across other websites.</li>
        <li>No accounts, logins, or forms that store your information.</li>
        <li>Nothing is sold or shared with third parties.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
      <p>Page views may be counted with a privacy-focused tool that does not use cookies or identify individual visitors. It records which pages are visited, not who visits them.</p>

      <h2>Embedded videos</h2>
      <p>Videos are hosted on YouTube. Nothing loads from YouTube until you press play. Once you do, YouTube's own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a> applies to that video.</p>

      <h2>Search</h2>
      <p>Site search runs entirely in your browser. Search terms are not sent anywhere.</p>

      <h2>Crime data on the map</h2>
      <p>The map uses public open data from city police departments. Incidents are aggregated to grid cells before publication, and no exact incident locations or personal information are shown. The map is for education and is not intended for operational, legal, or real-estate decisions.</p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, which may keep standard server logs, such as IP addresses, for security. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy can go to the email on the <a href="/about/">About</a> page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .prose { max-width: 44rem; }
  .prose h1 { margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: var(--t-lg); margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .prose ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: 0.4rem; max-width: var(--measure); }
</style>
